            "type": "text",
            "text": "{\"id\":\"TAC-675\",\"title\":\"Add internationalization (i18n) to Genesis\",\"description\":\"Enable Genesis to ship in multiple languages — product UI, shared chrome, and the public website.\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nUsers can view Genesis (and the main website) in their preferred locale, with a maintainable translation workflow for eng and content.\\n\\n## Branch strategy\\n\\nAll remaining i18n work lands on the long-lived `internationalization` branch (not directly on `main`).\\n\\n* Base feature PRs on `internationalization` (or merge stacked area branches into it).\\n* Keep pushing area tickets to `internationalization` until the epic is complete.\\n* Open one PR `internationalization` → `main` when the full epic is ready to ship.\\n\\nFoundation (<issue id=\\\"6b9fb302-6316-4470-ab52-5dfec691c6e0\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/agentuity/issue/TAC-676/i18n-base-framework-i18next\\\">TAC-676</issue> / <issue id=\\\"d0207113-5e63-48fb-8fe5-1b9a9ab524e0\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/agentuity/issue/TAC-677/i18n-app-shell-and-navigation\\\">TAC-677</issue>) already landed via #759; `internationalization` starts from that tip for follow-on work.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\n1. Land a base i18n framework (likely `i18next` + `react-i18next` for the web app).\\n2. Extract and translate copy area-by-area (product surfaces).\\n3. Internationalize the main marketing/docs website.\\n\\n## Out of scope (for now)\\n\\n* Translating model-generated chat content\\n* Full RTL layout polish (unless required by a first locale)\\n* Desktop-specific packaging beyond shared web strings\\n\\n## Child work\\n\\nSee sub-issues for framework setup, per-area product UI, and the main website.\",\"priority\":{\"value\":2,\"name\":\"High\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/agentuity/issue/TAC-675/add-internationalization-i18n-to-genesis\",\"gitBranchName\":\"tac-675-add-internationalization-i18n-to-genesis\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-17T20:46:20.687Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-07-31T23:49: